# Caddy reverse proxy for texloom with automatic HTTPS (Let's Encrypt).
# 1. Point a DNS name (e.g. texloom.example.org) at this machine.
# 2. Make ports 80 and 443 reachable (router port-forward if it's at home).
# 3. Replace the hostname below, then:  sudo caddy run --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
# Caddy obtains and renews the certificate itself and passes WebSockets through.
texloom.example.org {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8787
}
